  "ai_language_tip": "Start in Eastern Armenian (hy); Russian is widely understood and an easy fallback; English is common among younger staff in central Yerevan, weaker elsewhere.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Good in central Yerevan restaurants, hotels and tech-facing services; limited in clinics, garages and regions.",
  "politeness": "Warm and personal; formal 'Դուք'; open with 'Բարև Ձեզ'; address as 'պարոն …' / 'տիկին …'; close with 'Շնորհակալություն, ցտեսություն'.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings usually under first name, or surname (most end in -յան / -yan, not gendered); Latin spellings vary, so spell slowly.",
  "phone_tip": "National numbers 8 digits after 0: mobile 0XX XX XX XX (e.g. 091 12345678, 077, 093, 094, 095, 096, 098, 099, 041, 043, 055), Yerevan landline 010; international +374; WhatsApp, Viber and Telegram common.",
  "time_tip": "Spoken 'ութն անց կես' = 8:30 (half past eight, no German trap); written 24h ('19:30'); read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "Mobile numbers are read 3-2-2-2 ('իննսունմեկ, քսաներեք…'); Russian numerals also heard.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid restaurant peaks and calls after 21:00; Sundays for offices; 31 Dec–7 Jan holidays slow everything.",
  "closed_days": "Shops and restaurants open daily; offices closed weekends; holidays include 31 Dec–2 Jan, 6 January (Christmas), 28 January, 8 March, 24 April (remembrance day), 1 May, 9 May, 28 May, 5 July, 21 September, 31 December.",
